WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:19.025
Dr. Craven waited in Colin's room for a long time that afternoon.

2
00:00:19.026 --> 00:00:24.869
Finally the children returned to the house, and he looked Colin over very seriously.

3
00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:28.989
"You shouldn't have stayed out so long," Dr. Craven said.

4
00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:32.233
"You must not get over tired."

5
00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:37.007
"I'm not tired at all. Going outside has made me well.

6
00:00:37.008 --> 00:00:41.452
Tomorrow I'm going out in the morning, as well as the afternoon."

7
00:00:41.453 --> 00:00:45.712
The doctor frowned. "I'm not sure I can allow that.

8
00:00:45.713 --> 00:00:48.544
I'm afraid it would not be wise."

9
00:00:48.545 --> 00:00:52.100
"It would not be wise to try and stop me."

10
00:00:52.101 --> 00:00:56.632
Mary had noticed that Colin had a way of ordering others about.

11
00:00:56.633 --> 00:01:00.243
She had been that way too before she came to Misselthwaite.

12
00:01:00.244 --> 00:01:06.088
But now she knew better, and she felt that she must speak to Colin about his own manners.

13
00:01:06.089 --> 00:01:11.522
After the doctor left, she said, "I feel rather sorry for Dr. Craven."

14
00:01:11.523 --> 00:01:17.121
"So do I. He won't inherit Misselthwaite now that I'm getting well."

15
00:01:17.122 --> 00:01:21.051
"It must be hard to be polite to a boy who's always rude."

16
00:01:21.052 --> 00:01:24.332
Colin looked up. "Am I rude?"

17
00:01:24.333 --> 00:01:28.931
"Yes. Nobody has ever dared to do anything you don't like.

18
00:01:28.932 --> 00:01:32.866
Always having your way has made you rude and difficult."

19
00:01:32.867 --> 00:01:38.963
Colin frowned at her. He didn't like hearing bad things about himself.

20
00:01:38.964 --> 00:01:43.779
"Ben Weatherstaff and I are difficult too." Mary smiled at him.

21
00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:47.499
"But I'm not as bad as I was before I found the garden."

22
00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:50.829
"I don't want to be difficult, and I won't be."

23
00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:56.615
Now Colin was frowning with determination. Suddenly he smiled.

24
00:01:56.616 --> 00:02:01.460
"I'll stop being difficult if I go to the secret garden every day.

25
00:02:01.461 --> 00:02:04.951
There's magic in there. I'm sure of it."

26
00:02:04.952 --> 00:02:08.334
"So am I!" said Mary.

27
00:02:08.335 --> 00:02:13.495
In the months that followed, it did seem like magic was at work in the garden.

28
00:02:13.496 --> 00:02:18.016
Flowers pushed their way out of the earth and burst into bloom.

29
00:02:18.017 --> 00:02:21.252
The roses were flowering everywhere.

30
00:02:21.253 --> 00:02:26.335
Colin spent hours "watching things growing," as he liked to say.

31
00:02:26.336 --> 00:02:31.504
He watched the insects carrying tiny scraps of straw or food.

32
00:02:31.505 --> 00:02:36.446
Dickon introduced him to the ways of frogs and badgers and fish.

33
00:02:36.447 --> 00:02:40.307
There were so many things to look at in the secret garden.

34
00:02:40.308 --> 00:02:46.145
Colin began to believe there was magic not only in the garden but also in him.

35
00:02:46.146 --> 00:02:52.159
"Come, everyone," he said one day. "Stand here in a line."

36
00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:57.536
Mary, Dickon, and Ben stopped working in the garden and stood in front of Colin.

37
00:02:57.537 --> 00:03:03.526
"When I grow up, I am going to make great scientific discoveries," announced Colin.

38
00:03:03.527 --> 00:03:06.964
"I am going to begin now with this experiment.

39
00:03:06.965 --> 00:03:12.381
The magic in this garden has made me stand up and know that I'm going to live.

40
00:03:12.382 --> 00:03:17.699
Now I'm going to try to put more magic into myself so that I will grow strong.

41
00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:20.757
I don't know how to do this for sure.

42
00:03:20.758 --> 00:03:25.865
But perhaps if I keep thinking about it and calling it, the magic will come."

43
00:03:25.866 --> 00:03:29.939
"How will you do that?" asked Mary.

44
00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:33.901
"Every day, as often as I can, I'm going to say:

45
00:03:33.902 --> 00:03:38.629
'Magic is in me! Magic is making me well!

46
00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:41.616
I am going to be as strong as Dickon!'

47
00:03:41.617 --> 00:03:46.318
And you must say it too. Will you help me, Ben Weatherstaff?"

48
00:03:46.319 --> 00:03:52.541
"Yes," said the old gardener. "And now I'd like to see you walk."

49
00:03:52.542 --> 00:03:55.699
Colin set off with Dickon at his side.

50
00:03:55.700 --> 00:04:00.724
Mary and Ben followed along behind, as if they were in a parade.

51
00:04:00.725 --> 00:04:04.514
It was a parade that moved slowly but with dignity.

52
00:04:04.515 --> 00:04:07.952
Every few yards it stopped to rest.

53
00:04:07.953 --> 00:04:13.098
Colin leaned on Dickon's arm, but sometimes he walked by himself.

54
00:04:13.099 --> 00:04:19.628
"The magic is in me!" he kept saying. "The magic is making me strong!"

55
00:04:19.629 --> 00:04:22.628
They walked all around the garden.

56
00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:27.478
"I did it! The magic worked!" Colin exclaimed at the end.

57
00:04:27.479 --> 00:04:31.734
"What will Dr. Craven say?" asked Mary.

58
00:04:31.735 --> 00:04:36.528
"He won't say anything," said Colin, "because he won't be told.

59
00:04:36.529 --> 00:04:39.472
This will be the biggest secret of all.

60
00:04:39.473 --> 00:04:43.901
Every day I will go to and from the garden in my wheelchair.

61
00:04:43.902 --> 00:04:46.976
I won't have the servants whispering about me.

62
00:04:46.977 --> 00:04:51.682
I won't let my father hear about it until the experiment has succeeded.

63
00:04:51.683 --> 00:04:58.601
Then one day I will walk into his study and show him that I'm just like any other boy."

64
00:04:58.602 --> 00:05:04.833
"He'll think he's dreaming," said Mary. "He won't believe his eyes."

65
00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:09.658
"You'll grow so strong that you'll soon be boxing," said Ben.

66
00:05:09.659 --> 00:05:14.041
"You'll end up being the champion prizefighter of all England."

67
00:05:14.042 --> 00:05:19.406
Colin frowned at him. "No, Weatherstaff, that's not true.

68
00:05:19.407 --> 00:05:24.171
No matter how well the magic works, I will not be a prizefighter.

69
00:05:24.172 --> 00:05:27.508
I will be a scientific discoverer."

70
00:05:27.509 --> 00:05:34.607
"Oh, pardon, sir," said Ben. "I should have known it wasn't a joking matter."

71
00:05:34.608 --> 00:05:37.206
But his eyes twinkled.

72
00:05:37.207 --> 00:05:47.214
He could tell that Colin was already gaining strength and spirit.
